meta {
  name: Discord Notify
  type: http
  seq: 70
}

post {
  url: http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/v1/discord/notify
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "apikey": "",
    "message": "Test alert from OpenAlgo API",
    "wait_for_delivery": false
  }
}

docs {
  Post a message to the Discord channel whose webhook is saved on the /discord
  page. Discord alerts must be switched on at /alerts.

    "message":            the text, at most 2000 characters (Discord's limit)
    "wait_for_delivery":  false (default) queues the message and returns at once;
                          true posts it first and reports whether Discord took it

  Discord markdown in the message is kept. Mentions never ping anybody:
  @everyone, @here, users and roles are all suppressed.

  The webhook URL itself is never sent or returned by the API. Saving,
  replacing and removing it is done on the session-authenticated /discord page.
}
